## Type Patterns

### Discriminated Unions (for conditional props)
```typescript
// Component that's either a link OR a button
type {ComponentName}Props =
  | ({ as: 'link'; href: string } & AnchorHTMLAttributes<HTMLAnchorElement>)
  | ({ as?: 'button' } & ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>)
```

### Required vs Optional Props
```typescript
interface Props {
  // Required - component won't work without it
  title: string

  // Optional with default - has sensible fallback
  variant?: 'default' | 'primary'  // @default 'default'

  // Optional without default - truly optional
  subtitle?: string
}
```

### Callback Props
```typescript
interface Props {
  /**
   * Called when the component value changes
   * @param value - The new value
   */
  onChange?: (value: string) => void

  /**
   * Called when the component is clicked
   * @param event - The click event
   */
  onClick?: (event: React.MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>) => void
}
```

